id: pm-qwuber
title: "ADR: agent identity model — stable author namespace plus structured harness, model, and session provenance"
description: Decide the stable author and structured harness/model provenance contract while keeping invocation session identifiers transient and non-durable.
type: Decision
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[7]: adr,agent-ux,"area:sdk",author,governance,identity,provenance
created_at: "2026-07-25T12:24:02.830Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-26T11:28:28.522Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-25T20:06:39.645Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "The decision states whether model belongs in the author string or in structured provenance fields, with the rejected options and their reasons recorded; The decision names every provenance field, its type, its cardinality expectations, and its absence semantics (a missing model must never degrade the author to unknown); The decision states explicitly that detected identity is an unverified claim and may never be used as an authorization input, deferring verified identity to pm-u14c; The decision states the privacy contract: which identity dimensions may reach telemetry, in what hashed form, and which must never leave the machine; The decision states the compatibility rule for workspaces written before model capture existed, so old streams stay valid and verifiable; A superseding or amending decision is required before any later change to the recorded identity shape"
goal: project management = context management
objective: "Decide, once and in writing, what an automatically detected agent identity consists of and what it is never permitted to assert"
value: "Attribution that distinguishes harness from model is the precondition for fleet analytics, per-model context profiles, and any trust decision about who may hold a claim"
impact: Locks the on-disk provenance shape for every future history entry; a wrong choice here is expensive to reverse because history is immutable by design
outcome: "Every later identity change — model capture, signatures, fleet analytics, per-model context profiles — extends one decided data model instead of renegotiating it in immutable history"
why_now: Model capture is about to be implemented; identity fields are append-only history and cannot be renamed later without a redaction workflow
parent: pm-m2u1
risk: medium
confidence: 75
resolution: Accepted durable identity is stable author plus optional harness/model/model-source; session signals remain transient and non-serializable.
expected_result: "A written, privacy-bounded, backward-compatible identity decision governs SDK, CLI, MCP, history, and telemetry."
actual_result: "ADR amended and implemented; raw branch-local session fields were scrubbed and all 2,028 history streams verify without drift."
