  "2026-07-25T18:18:16.583Z","harness:codex","Implementation start: active in the cohesive automatic identity platform PR spanning the identity ADR, structured SDK provenance, precedence-safe observation, declarative harness registry, MCP/plugin configuration, and token-minimal help guidance. Duplicate check covered all 2,028 tracker items and live GitHub reports; no new item created."
  "2026-07-25T19:14:50.527Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: accepted agent identity ADR is now embodied in shared SDK/runtime contracts. History records author_source independently from observed agent_harness, agent_model, agent_model_source, and local-only transient_session_signal. Telemetry emits only presence at minimal capture and installation-keyed harness/model hashes plus fixed model-source enums at redacted/max; session is never emitted. Verification: 6,376 tests passed with 100/100/100/100 coverage, strict 100% docstring/static/API/token gates passed, secret scan clean, packed isolated acceptance passed."
  "2026-07-25T19:51:54.821Z","harness:codex","Review amendment: session identifiers are transient host context only and are no longer serialized to durable history or telemetry. Exact branch-local history streams were scrubbed of the mistakenly persisted top-level field. Additional review hardening covers bounded settings validation, executable-basename argv matching, inherited environment values, cached descriptor normalization, deterministic telemetry tests, and failure-safe registration cleanup."
  "2026-07-25T20:06:38.334Z","harness:codex","Final evidence: PR #713 exact head 446d00ae passed all 6,376 tests and 100/100/100/100 coverage (44,010 statements, 31,205 branches, 8,996 functions, 42,752 lines); strict 100% docstring/static/token/API gates; packed unrelated-directory SDK and CLI acceptance; CodeQL, DeepScan with zero findings, Semgrep, Trivy, TruffleHog, CodeFactor, Hound, Windows, compatibility, smokes, and benchmarks. All 13 CodeRabbit findings were individually fixed/dispositioned/reacted and every thread is resolved. Follow-up CodeRabbit and Greptile requests reached external free-review limits after the complete first review."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-26T11:27:54.105Z","harness:claude-code","Live signal census, 2026-07-26 Claude Code session, taken from the actual process environment rather than from the descriptor table.\n\nPresent: CLAUDECODE, CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID, CLAUDE_CODE_BRIDGE_SESSION_ID, CLAUDE_CODE_CHILD_SESSION, CLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT=cli, CLAUDE_CODE_EXECPATH, CLAUDE_PID, CLAUDE_EFFORT=xhigh, TERM_PROGRAM=ghostty.\n\nThree consequences for this ADR's dimension list.\n\n1. The thinking level is available and unrepresentable. CLAUDE_EFFORT carries exactly the value the mandate asks identity to include ('Opus 5 xhigh' — the xhigh half is sitting in the environment right now). HarnessSignalDescriptor (src/core/shared/author.ts:35-39) declares three signal kinds: environment_keys, model_environment_keys, session_environment_keys. There is no effort or reasoning-level kind, so this is not an unpopulated field — there is no field. Adding it is a schema change to the descriptor contract, which is why it belongs to this ADR rather than to a capture item.\n\n2. The descriptor schema is per-harness rows against a fixed dimension set. All eight built-in descriptors repeat the same three keys. A fourth dimension currently means editing every row plus DetectedAgentIdentity plus HistoryEntry plus the writer. That coupling is the reason dimensions have been added one at a time and is worth deciding against explicitly.\n\n3. Sub-agent lineage is a real distinction this environment already exposes and the contract does not model. CLAUDE_CODE_BRIDGE_SESSION_ID and CLAUDE_CODE_CHILD_SESSION are both set: this process is a child of another agent session. The descriptor reads only CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID, so a forked sub-agent and its parent are indistinguishable even before the transient-session decision applies. If the ADR keeps session identifiers non-durable, it should say what — if anything — records that two mutations came from different agents in the same fleet, because pm-z8qd4k shows the operational cost of the answer being 'nothing'."
