close_reason: "Implemented and verified in PR #713 with complete local, packed-consumer, hosted-gate, and review evidence."
body: "## Decision\n\nAccepted: keep `author` as the stable effective principal and record durable runtime observation separately as optional `agent_harness`, `agent_model`, and `agent_model_source` history fields. Widening author to `harness:<harness>/<model>` is rejected because it breaks existing equality filters, increases cardinality, and conflates stable selection with volatile observation. Signed principals remain deferred to pm-u14c.\n\nSession identifiers are accepted only as transient host input to `DetectedAgentIdentity`. They are deliberately excluded from `HistoryEntry`, item metadata, logs, and telemetry because a durable or exported session identifier creates correlation and privacy risk without improving stable project context.\n\n## Contract\n\n- `agent_harness?: string`: normalized low-cardinality harness namespace. Missing means no bounded signal matched.\n- `agent_model?: string`: bounded model identifier exactly observed from an allowed signal. Missing means unknown and never changes the effective author to `unknown`.\n- `agent_model_source?: override | environment | mcp_client | argv`: fixed-cardinality provenance for the model value. It is absent whenever `agent_model` is absent.\n- `session?: string` on transient detection results only: bounded invocation identifier available to the current embedding host and never serialized.\n\nAuthor precedence remains explicit argument, `PM_AUTHOR`, configured default, detected harness, then `unknown`. Detection always executes independently, so asserted or configured authors may still carry observed durable agent fields. These observations are unverified claims: they are attribution/context only and MUST NOT authorize access, ownership takeover, or privileged operations.\n\n## Privacy and compatibility\n\nTelemetry may emit only presence booleans at minimal capture, or installation-keyed one-way hashes of harness/model plus the fixed model-source enum at redacted/max capture. Session identifiers must never enter durable history or leave the process. Legacy entries without the optional durable fields remain valid and replay/verifiability semantics are unchanged.\n\nThis amendment was made during PR review before merge. The exact affected branch-local history streams were mechanically scrubbed of the mistakenly serialized transient field; PM replay and history-drift validation must remain green. Any future author-string incorporation, durable-field rename, cardinality expansion, session persistence/export, or authorization use requires an explicit superseding or amending Decision item linked to this ADR."
